{"id": "Mercury_414504", "question": "Students have a rock sample that may contain the mineral hematite. They know that hematite has a red or rusty streak. How can the students determine the color of the streak in the rock sample?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): use a rock with the known mineral to strike the sample", "B): rub the sample on a piece of unglazed clay tile", "C): use a file to break off a piece of the sample", "D): scratch the sample with an iron nail"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "The students know that hematite has a red or rusty streak. To determine the color of the streak in the rock sample, they need to find a way to make the sample produce a streak. This can be done by rubbing the sample on a piece of unglazed clay tile. The clay tile will produce a streak that is the same color as the mineral in the sample. This is a common technique used in geology to identify minerals.\nThe correct answer is (B): rub the sample on a piece of unglazed clay tile.\nThe best answer is B.<|eot_id|>", "initial_cot_probs": [0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0], "initial_probs": [0.002669377252459526, 0.9503640532493591, 0.007256118580698967, 0.03684961423277855], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "cot_step": "The students know that hematite has a red or rusty streak.", "segmented_cot": ["The students know that hematite has a red or rusty streak.", "To determine the color of the streak in the rock sample, they need to find a way to make the sample produce a streak.", "This can be done by rubbing the sample on a piece of unglazed clay tile.", "The clay tile will produce a streak that is the same color as the mineral in the sample.", "This is a common technique used in geology to identify minerals.", "The correct answer is (B): rub the sample on a piece of unglazed clay tile.", "The best answer is B.<|eot_id|>"], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "B): rub the sample on a piece of un", "probs": [0.002669377252459526, 0.9503640532493591, 0.007256118580698967, 0.03684961